# .gitignore — what must never enter this repository.
#
# Two entries here are privacy controls, not housekeeping, and they are the reason this file is
# reviewed rather than generated:
#
#   * AUDIO (*.wav, *.flac, and the raw-capture scratch paths below) — rules.md R-14 and R-21. No raw
#     audio persists anywhere by default, and research audio never enters this repository or default
#     cloud storage. Manifests carry hashes and IDs; the audio itself stays in controlled research
#     storage under the consent ledger. Git makes deletion effectively impossible: a `git rm` leaves
#     the blob in every clone's history and in every fork, so a single committed sample converts a
#     retention promise into something the team cannot honour. There is no "just this once" here.
#
#   * MODEL WEIGHTS (*.onnx, *.pth, *.pt, *.ckpt) — architecture.md section 5.1 and rules.md R-42/R-51.
#     The parity set tracks a model by its SHA-256, recorded in calibration.json and the release
#     manifest. A committed .onnx puts an unversioned artifact *outside* that set: two tiers could then
#     load different bytes while both reporting the same Git commit, and the dual-tier parity claim
#     would be false in exactly the way nobody thinks to check. Model artifacts are released with a
#     hash and a manifest, not committed alongside source.
#
# Everything else below is ordinary build/tooling noise, plus the secret-bearing files that rules.md
# R-34 forbids in Git.

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Virtualenvs. The `.venv*` glob deliberately covers the scratch `.venv-verify/` at the repo root:
# a committed interpreter tree is ~100 MB of files that also happen to shadow the pinned 3.12
# environment the parity set depends on (gateway/requirements.txt, decision D-10).
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
env/

# ── Node / PWA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Infrastructure ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
cdk.out/
*.cdk.staging/
.cdk.staging/
cdk.context.json
infra/cdk/**/*.js
infra/cdk/**/*.d.ts

# Rendered IAM policy documents. The sources in infra/iam/ carry `<AWS_ACCOUNT_ID>` placeholders and
# ARE committed; scripts/render_iam_policies.py substitutes them into this directory, so its contents
# embed a real account id. The generated directory also ships its own `.gitignore` containing `*` —
# belt and braces, so the protection survives someone deleting this line, and holds even before this
# file is read (the renderer writes it on every run).
infra/iam/rendered/

# ── Secrets (rules.md R-34: no secrets in Git, images, or the client) ──────────────────────────────
# gateway/.env.example IS committed — it is all obvious placeholders. gateway/.env is not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
gateway/.env
scorer/.env
pwa/.env
*.secret
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*_secret.json
credentials
.aws/
# A committed key file is the single finding secret-scan.yml exists to prevent reaching `main`.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# mkcert-generated local TLS material. The local CA is a *trusted root* on every device it is
# installed on (architecture.md section 5) — committing its key hands anyone who clones this repo the
# ability to mint certificates the demo phone will trust.
#
# NOTE THE TRAILING `/*`, AND DO NOT "TIDY" IT TO `**/certs/`. Excluding the *directory* also excludes
# everything under it permanently: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so
# `!**/certs/README.md` below would silently do nothing and `infra/compose/certs/README.md` — the
# instructions for generating this material — could never be committed. A fresh clone would then have
# no certs directory and no way to find out what belongs in it. Excluding the *contents* keeps the
# negation working.
**/certs/*
!**/certs/README.md
!**/certs/.gitkeep
rootCA.pem
rootCA-key.pem
*-key.pem
*+*.pem
mkcert*

# ── Audio — see the header. rules.md R-14, R-21. ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.opus
*.aac
*.pcm
*.raw
*.sph
# Scratch capture directories people create while debugging the frame parser. Named explicitly
# because "I'll delete it before committing" is not a control.
captures/
recordings/
audio_dump/
*_capture/

# ── Model weights and large artifacts — see the header. architecture.md section 5.1. ───────────────
*.onnx
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.tflite
*.pb
*.h5
# Training scratch. Checkpoints belong in the model release directory with a SHA-256, not in Git.
ml/runs/
ml/checkpoints/
ml/wandb/
mlruns/

# Dataset payloads. datasets/manifest/manifest.parquet IS the tracked artifact (Pair B) — it holds
# hashes and IDs, never audio, and scripts/validate_manifest.py is what keeps that true.
datasets/raw/
datasets/audio/
datasets/**/*.tar
datasets/**/*.tar.gz
datasets/**/*.zip

# ── Scratch extractions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# _part2_extract.txt is a text extraction of the source runbook PDF held at the repo root while the
# planning docs were written. The authoritative copy is
# PS104_team_document_set/SIH26104_Phase1-3_Implementation_Runbook.md; the extract is lossy OCR and
# committing it would create a second, subtly-wrong copy of a normative document.
_part2_extract.txt
*_extract.txt

# ── Editor / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
